/A 1468 0 R
/Alt (Diagram illustrating strategies for longevity. Panel A shows current strategies like genetic manipulation, dietary restriction, targeting senescence, partial reprogramming, and drugs, as tested on C. Elegans, Drosophila melanogaster, and Mus musculus. Panel B depicts a single-cell atlas for aging, with cell type map, aging timeline from young to old, and cell-type specificity factors like muscle, fat, immune, and neuron cells. The conclusion points to precise interventions for longevity.)
